# Cursor Rules — Hemsedal Packing Website

> This file configures Cursor IDE behavior for this project. Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root for full context.

---

## Project Identity

A 3D winter landscape website for a Hemsedal ski trip packing checklist. Next.js 16 + React 19 + @react-three/fiber + three.js. Inspired by basement.studio. The app lives in `websitehemsedal/`.

---

## Always Do

- Read the target file **and its imports** before editing.
- Read `Plans/03 - world-map.md` before making any spatial/placement decisions.
- Run `npm run format` and `npm run lint` (from `websitehemsedal/`) after making changes.
- Use Leva `useControls` for any tunable shader parameter (sky, fog, grading) — never hardcode.
- Keep CSS palette in `src/styles/tokens.css` in sync with Blender vertex colors and shader uniforms.
- Update `Plans/03 - world-map.md` AND `src/lib/worldMap.ts` when moving any landmark or zone.
- Export geometry changes through Blender: `assets/blender/hemsedal-landscape.blend` → glTF → `public/models/`.
- Use the path alias `@/*` for imports from `src/`.
- Use `import type` for type-only imports.
- Preserve the `<!-- BEGIN:nextjs-agent-rules -->` block in `websitehemsedal/AGENTS.md`.
- Commit with the Mistral Vibe co-author trailer:
  ```
  Generated by Mistral Vibe.
  Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>
  ```

---

## Never Do

- Don't install Tailwind, Sass, Emotion, styled-components, or any CSS framework.
- Don't mount a second `<Canvas>` — there is exactly one, in `Scene.tsx`.
- Don't generate terrain, landmark, or prop geometry in code — it's all authored in Blender.
- Don't add `"use client"` to a component that doesn't need it (hooks, browser APIs, R3F).
- Don't change the color palette in `tokens.css` without repainting vertex colors in Blender.
- Don't move a landmark without updating `Plans/03 - world-map.md` and `src/lib/worldMap.ts`.
- Don't remove the Next.js agent-rules block from `websitehemsedal/AGENTS.md`.
- Don't use `any` type without a comment explaining why.
- Don't hardcode camera positions, sky colors, or grading values — use Leva + `cameraPositions.ts`.

---

## File Conventions

| Pattern | Rule |
|---|---|
| Components | PascalCase (`World.tsx`), colocated with CSS Module if needed |
| Utilities / lib | camelCase (`worldMap.ts`, `cameraPositions.ts`) |
| Shaders | `*.vert.ts` / `*.frag.ts` exporting template string constants |
| Styles | `tokens.css` (global), `base.css` (reset), `*.module.css` (scoped) |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE exports (e.g., `WORLD_BOUNDS`, `ZONES`) |

---

## Key Files

| File | What it does |
|---|---|
| `Plans/03 - world-map.md` | World map — coordinates, zones, landmark positions, camera shots |
| `assets/blender/hemsedal-landscape.blend` | Blender scene — source of truth for all geometry |
| `websitehemsedal/public/models/hemsedal-landscape.glb` | Optimized glTF export |
| `websitehemsedal/src/components/Scene.tsx` | Canvas mount, scene composition, Leva panel |
| `websitehemsedal/src/components/World.tsx` | Loads Blender glTF scene via `useGLTF` |
| `websitehemsedal/src/components/Sky.tsx` | Sky dome + gradient + sun glow shader |
| `websitehemsedal/src/components/FreeFlyCamera.tsx` | Dev-only fly camera (WASD + mouse) |
| `websitehemsedal/src/lib/shaders/sky.vert.ts` | GLSL sky vertex shader |
| `websitehemsedal/src/lib/shaders/sky.frag.ts` | GLSL sky fragment shader (gradient + sun) |
| `websitehemsedal/src/lib/worldMap.ts` | Code mirror of world map: zones, landmarks, bounds |
| `websitehemsedal/src/lib/cameraPositions.ts` | Hero camera shots |
| `websitehemsedal/src/styles/tokens.css` | Design tokens (the brand) |
| `websitehemsedal/src/styles/base.css` | CSS reset + canvas/content layers |

---

## Commands (run from `websitehemsedal/`)

```bash
npm run dev          # Dev server
npm run build        # Build + type check
npm run lint         # ESLint
npm run format       # Prettier write

# Blender export pipeline
npx @gltf-transform/cli optimize public/models/hemsedal-landscape.glb public/models/hemsedal-landscape.glb --compress draco --texture-compress ktx2
```

---

## Phase Context

Currently in **Phase 1 — Landscape MVP (Blender-authored)**. Terrain, landmarks, and props are sculpted in Blender, exported as glTF, and loaded via `World.tsx`. Sky shader, fog, free-fly camera, and color grading are in place. Next steps: finalize Blender scene, bake lighting, save camera positions. See `Plans/02 - plan-phase-1-landscape-mvp.md` for the full phase plan and `Plans/03 - world-map.md` for all coordinates.
